AB  - Currently, retrieval-augmented generation methods that optimize document retrieval through knowledge graph expansion still face the following challenge: during the graph expansion process, the use of an indiscriminate fixed-hop expansion strategy fails to dynamically adjust the expansion length and direction based on the actual effectiveness of the expanded paths, leading to the introduction of significant noise while also risking incomplete coverage of reasoning paths. To suppress noise introduction while ensuring the integrity of reasoning paths, this paper proposes Smart KG-RAG: Smart Knowledge Graph Guided Retrieval Augmentation. This method quantifies path quality from three complementary dimensions—with marginal contribution (i.e., the proportion of unique information contributed by the path and the success rate of expansion per hop) serving as the dominant signal, semantic relevance as the secondary indicator, and structural consistency as a lightweight regularizer—and dynamically adjusts the expansion length and direction on the knowledge graph accordingly, achieving adaptive node expansion. In this way, it expands document chunks highly relevant to the query while effectively suppressing the noise caused by further expansion of low-utility paths. Furthermore, by reorganizing and reranking the expanded document chunks, it constructs a knowledge document containing a complete reasoning path, providing large language models with contextually coherent and structurally clear support. We validate the effectiveness of our model on two classic question answering datasets: MuSiQue and HotpotQA. The F1 scores for response quality improve by 1.8% and 3.0%, respectively, while those for retrieval quality improve by 0.6% and 1.5%, respectively. Additionally, a stratified analysis on the MuSiQue dataset, which includes hop-number annotations, shows that the F1 scores for response quality improve by 0.9%, 2.2%, and 4.2% on 2-hop, 3-hop, and 4-hop questions, respectively, with the improvement increasing as question complexity grows. This further validates the effectiveness and robustness of the model on complex multi-hop reasoning tasks.
